  "answer": "This looks like a known limitation, not a new bug. In terminal#9167 a user saw the same thing: after saving from the settings UI, the order of things in settings.json was lost. The maintainers closed it as a duplicate of the umbrella issue #8991, because Terminal has no good in-place editing for the settings file. On every save it re-serializes the whole document, so keys such as actions and keybindings can move and comments can be lost. The tickets I was shown give no fix or workaround, so I can't promise one. Please follow #8991 for progress. In the meantime, expect the file to be rewritten whenever settings are saved, for example when you add a shortcut in the UI. To keep diffs readable, compare the files after a normalizing step, or save once to get the new order and commit that as your baseline."
 },
